  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This activity Support for development of an Index to capture the social, economic and political impact of the World-Wide-Web, and also increase Web access through regulatory reform: World-Wide-Web Foundation (W3F) Grant is a component of Support for development of an Index to capture the social, economic and political impact of the World-Wide-Web, and increase Web access through regulatory reform. reported by FCDO with a funding type of 111 - Not for profit organisation and a budget of &#xa3;1,250,000. This project benefits Developing countries, unspecified. It works in the following sector(s): Democratic participation and civil society, Media and free flow of information.</narrative>
  </description>
